For $C=N,O$, let $T^C_{S,c,r}\ge0$ for every schedule, cell and label,
and require

$$
\sum_{r=0}^6T^C_{S,c,r}=w_S\quad\text{for every cell }c,\qquad
\sum_Sw_S=1,\qquad
p_b(r)=\sum_ST^C_{S,c_C(b,S),r}.
\tag{154.1}
$$

All seven labels are permitted in every cell, including unqueried labels.
There are 22 schedules, 73 $N$ cells and 58 $O$ cells, hence 511 and 406
terminal coordinates. Eliminating $w$ gives respectively 52 and 37
independent equalities: one difference for every cell after its schedule's
first cell, and one global normalization. Independence follows because
each difference contains a cell absent from all other differences for
that schedule, while normalization has nonzero total mass.

These are precisely the full finite classes, by
[Proposition 140.3](KBONACCI_SELF_CALIBRATING_ACQUISITION_RESOURCES_CONTINUATION_II.md#140-original-sources-and-complete-common-budget-allocations).
Static reversed or repeated $N$ queries do not supply additional finite
output functions; sorting or deleting a repeated observation represents
the law without increasing the hard bound. This does not make an actual
repeated request uncounted. Write $\Pi_C$ for the set of profiles having
an allocation (154.1) with $\operatorname{TV}(p_b,\eta_b)\le e$ for every
word. A single allocation serves all words and events.

